public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic

/-!
# Separated local rings with principal maximal ideal

A local ring with a chosen generator of its maximal ideal has unit-power factorizations below
a finite maximal-ideal order. Hausdorff separation and nonvanishing of every generator power
then give domain and discrete valuation ring structures. No Noetherian hypothesis is imposed.

## Extraction basis

Transferred existing declarations from
`R5Lab/AlgebraicGeometry/LocalRing/SeparatedPrincipal.lean` at revision
`79307ff88f07d34fd5c3edb859f799c55e38f290`, source SHA-256
`fb4fd950fd8a455c23d5b40ed3b689cd553d9c7fed4b00f131f3de1c44a235b6`, lines 18–84.
The stated hypotheses and chosen maps are retained; declarations use native mathematical
namespaces and canonical carriers. Source correspondence is separate from native Lean validation.
